    "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
    "markdown": "Managing focus with ADHD requires `breaking tasks into tiny steps and reducing distractions in your environment`.\n\n### Quick Focus Strategies\n\n- **Use the Pomodoro Technique:** Work for 20 minutes, then rest for 5 minutes. Short timers make big tasks feel easy.\n- **Clear your desk:** Remove everything except what you need for the current task. Out of sight means out of mind.\n- **Wear headphones:** Play instrumental music, white noise, or brown noise to block out sudden sounds.\n- **Write down stray thoughts:** Keep a notepad nearby. When a random idea pops up, write it down and go back to work.\n- **Break tasks apart:** Instead of \"clean the room,\" make the step \"pick up three shirts.\"\n\n### Brain Care\n\n- **Eat protein:** A high-protein breakfast helps your brain make chemicals for attention.\n- **Move your body:** Take a quick walk or do jumping jacks before starting a hard task.\n- **Sleep well:** Tired brains have a much harder time staying on track.\n\nIf you want, tell me:\n\n- What **specific task** are you trying to do right now?\n- What is **distracting you** the most?\n\nI can give you a quick, custom plan to get started.",
